{"author":"pszypowicz","children":[{"author":"nfRfqX5n","children":[{"author":"vaylian","children":[{"author":"hgoel","children":[{"author":"thejazzman","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:51:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790167873,"id":49815308,"options":[],"parent_id":49815254,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It is most certainly the kind of subtle bug the LLMs love to slip in and burn you in production<p>Not sure what y\u2019all are thinking with these unwritten conspiracy theories that begin and end with \u201cit\u2019s intentional\u201d","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:44:22.000Z","created_at_i":1790167462,"id":49815254,"options":[],"parent_id":49815246,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Vibe coding","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"jpitz","children":[{"author":"kriro","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:22:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790169745,"id":49815713,"options":[],"parent_id":49815259,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Get more people to turn on telemetry.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"zigzag312","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T09:03:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790240590,"id":49828073,"options":[],"parent_id":49815259,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Publish new features first to clients that provide feedback, so rollout can be stopped, if there&#x27;s an issue with new version. Telemetry off effectively prioritizes stability over speed of recieving new versions.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:45:07.000Z","created_at_i":1790167507,"id":49815259,"options":[],"parent_id":49815246,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Assuming that it&#x27;s intentional, what&#x27;s the motivation?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:43:41.000Z","created_at_i":1790167421,"id":49815246,"options":[],"parent_id":49815144,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Can you think of a bug that makes sense in this case?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"kennethops","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:45:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790167546,"id":49815265,"options":[],"parent_id":49815144,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I like to give my graces to people and the companies who are typically not trillions of dollars. Have an incredible amount of resources that many countries would like to have, with fewer of the obligations. I&#x27;m going to chalk this up to its intended","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"serial_dev","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:47:01.000Z","created_at_i":1790167621,"id":49815273,"options":[],"parent_id":49815144,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Someone on the Claude Code team is probably wondering the same...","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Razengan","children":[{"author":"jaapz","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:04:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790168655,"id":49815459,"options":[],"parent_id":49815276,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"many of these can also be chalked up to the fact that all of their products are extremely vibed","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"nibbleyou","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:06:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790168807,"id":49815501,"options":[],"parent_id":49815276,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I cannot set a password for login, on logging in it says we&#x27;ve sent a login code but it&#x27;s a link instead...","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:47:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790167633,"id":49815276,"options":[],"parent_id":49815144,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Claude&#x2F;Anthropic has been sus from the start:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.thatprivacyguy.com&#x2F;blog&#x2F;anthropic-spyware&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.thatprivacyguy.com&#x2F;blog&#x2F;anthropic-spyware&#x2F;</a><p>+ not letting users change their email, or remove their payment methods, etc.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:34:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790166853,"id":49815144,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Crazy part is: can\u2019t tell if this intended or a bug","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"chrisjj","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:34:56.000Z","created_at_i":1790166896,"id":49815154,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Vibe-coding at its best.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"tjoff","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:45:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790167555,"id":49815266,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Nice find, though I&#x27;d rather read the prompt that was used to write this article. It is about ten times longer than it needs to and is quite painful to read.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"sandrello","children":[{"author":"hgoel","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:53:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790168005,"id":49815335,"options":[],"parent_id":49815277,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Yep, especially with long contexts (and moreso if the last thing you were working on in the same context involved telemetry too). AI sneaks in weird conditions like this and then does the entire &quot;You&#x27;re absolutely right&quot; thing if you&#x27;re paying enough attention to catch it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"crazygringo","children":[{"author":"q3k","children":[{"author":"crazygringo","children":[{"author":"abathologist","children":[{"author":"crazygringo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:07:06.000Z","created_at_i":1790176026,"id":49817310,"options":[],"parent_id":49816575,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"No, people seem to be adopting simplistic narratives and then slotting the facts wherever they most conveniently fit into their narrative.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:17:48.000Z","created_at_i":1790173068,"id":49816575,"options":[],"parent_id":49816181,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"People are just paying attention to what is happening the world.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"shimman","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:22:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790180550,"id":49818443,"options":[],"parent_id":49816181,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"You say cynical but employees at these companies also lie just as much as their leaders. It&#x27;s good to be skeptical of people that want to capture generational wealth while destroying the planet.<p>People aren&#x27;t cynical enough here.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:50:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790171439,"id":49816181,"options":[],"parent_id":49815734,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Wow people are cynical here.<p>No matter what happens to be the truth, HNers have a cynical narrative to fit it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:23:48.000Z","created_at_i":1790169828,"id":49815734,"options":[],"parent_id":49815449,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; It seems to be exactly the opposite, a &quot;fully human error&quot;<p>&quot;LLMize the succeses, humanize the failures.&quot; is the PR strategy at play here. Anything goes well it&#x27;s because AI did it, anything goes bad it&#x27;s because a human didn&#x27;t catch it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"fg137","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:44:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790171080,"id":49816090,"options":[],"parent_id":49815449,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"One thing I do know is that an Anthropic employee is definitely NOT going to blame this on the model they are using.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"pasteleft","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:29:05.000Z","created_at_i":1790191745,"id":49821260,"options":[],"parent_id":49815449,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I don&#x27;t understand what you are talking about. Vibecoding IS a human error.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:03:28.000Z","created_at_i":1790168608,"id":49815449,"options":[],"parent_id":49815277,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It seems to be exactly the opposite, a &quot;fully human error&quot;:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49815363\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49815363</a><p>Nothing to do with AI patches at all, nor was it a bug. It was intentional human behavior, a temporary rollout setting, that seems to have made sense.<p>But I guess that doesn&#x27;t fit the &quot;narrative&quot;.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"tpurves","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:15:49.000Z","created_at_i":1790169349,"id":49815614,"options":[],"parent_id":49815277,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Except that, and this I find slightly amusing,  is a situation where they definitely don&#x27;t want to publicly blame the ai model when there are mistakes.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Agentlien","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:16:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790169387,"id":49815625,"options":[],"parent_id":49815277,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I used to actively use Msty for local models because it just worked and had a lot of nice advanced features. A few months ago they released their beta version of a Claw-like UI and mentioned using a version of it to develop Msty itself. Well, that was around the time I stopped using Msty because every update started breaking things and two updates in a row included bugs which wiped all my configs, chats, and history.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"HotHotLava","children":[{"author":"code_runner","children":[{"author":"code_runner","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:04:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790172270,"id":49816373,"options":[],"parent_id":49816345,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"ps: apparently thats not how you spell emblematic - but I&#x27;m actually glad to leave a little humanity around given the topic :D","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"t-writescode","children":[{"author":"quintu5","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:04:18.000Z","created_at_i":1790186658,"id":49820092,"options":[],"parent_id":49817519,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Except it\u2019s not a new issue. This is just the feature that made it a conversation topic.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:22:45.000Z","created_at_i":1790176965,"id":49817519,"options":[],"parent_id":49816345,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Or it\u2019s as simple as \u201chey, they don\u2019t want telemetry? Cool, we\u2019ll turn off all the extra phoning home\u201d and their feature flag code uses the same paths as telemetry because it\u2019s the same endpoint, etc.<p>Oops, easy mistake!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"archonis","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:28:26.000Z","created_at_i":1790177306,"id":49817601,"options":[],"parent_id":49816345,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Good thing they don&#x27;t apply the same standards to security sandboxes.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:03:08.000Z","created_at_i":1790172188,"id":49816345,"options":[],"parent_id":49816005,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"a &quot;feature&quot; that every user has asked for - which is the equivalent of changing claude.md to agents.md - and the release isn&#x27;t even smooth because the telemetry isn&#x27;t wired up quite right.<p>for an organization that is being used as a model for new agentic software development practices.... and every software exec on earth is trying to reshape their organizations after - its a pretty stupid bug for a feature that should&#x27;ve been straightforward in the first place + took forever for them to get around to.<p>its just kind of emblamatic of the rough edges that exist EVEN FOR SIMPLE THINGS whenever human judgement is totally removed the equation.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"ares623","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T02:00:44.000Z","created_at_i":1790215244,"id":49825278,"options":[],"parent_id":49816005,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"and the enshittification lives on","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"csomar","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T06:29:37.000Z","created_at_i":1790231377,"id":49826959,"options":[],"parent_id":49816005,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The issue is that this is the thing that got \u201cnoticed\u201d. The problem is that your program behavior is now unpredictable. Anything can happen!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:39:32.000Z","created_at_i":1790170772,"id":49816005,"options":[],"parent_id":49815277,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&quot;extremely severe&quot; - aren&#x27;t we laying it on a bit thick here? The whole impact seems to be that users who have telemetry turned off got this feature ~2 days later, when the bug was noticed.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:47:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790167633,"id":49815277,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Based on my experience with these tools so far, this seems exactly the kind of subtle but extremely severe bug that sneaks in when you start piling up layers of AI generated patches to a codebase without caring too much about the code.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Traubenfuchs","children":[{"author":"geophph","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:14:32.000Z","created_at_i":1790172872,"id":49816532,"options":[],"parent_id":49815289,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Turns out AGI boils down to two markdown files:<p>claude-md-or-agents-md<p>claude-md-and-agents-md","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:49:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790167755,"id":49815289,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Issue 95690, opened 3 days ago, 500k+ engineers, a simple CLI...<p>AGI was reached like 2 weeks ago, latest claude 5.x models rule supreme and software engineering is solved?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"lucfranken","children":[{"author":"fg137","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:21:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790169670,"id":49815692,"options":[],"parent_id":49815297,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This is what&#x27;s written in their release notes for 2.1.277:<p>&gt; Added AGENTS.md support: in a project with no CLAUDE.md, Claude Code reads AGENTS.md instead<p>My dumb brain tells me none of this is rolled out progressively (as of that version). You either have it or not.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"nijave","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:38:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790170726,"id":49815994,"options":[],"parent_id":49815297,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s been like this at least months. I turned telemetry off a few months ago and it basically prevented all stages rollouts of new features from working.<p>Anthropic commonly gates behind feature flags that require telemetry until they&#x27;re &quot;promoted&quot; and defaulted on.<p>A little bit annoying you can&#x27;t manually control the flags without telemetry but I think the title is a bit click bait.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:50:03.000Z","created_at_i":1790167803,"id":49815297,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Isn&#x27;t that how they just release all features? So they can do progressive roll outs and telemetry on issues with it?<p>Not sure if they later move the code from inside the flag check to the main code or that they keep the flag check.<p>But if they would keep all features behind a flag that would not make most sense as you then would have not many features without telemetry.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"vorticalbox","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:51:31.000Z","created_at_i":1790167891,"id":49815311,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I use cursor and claude, its kinda annoying having to have the same skills in both so I made a ~&#x2F;.agents&#x2F;skills folder then ln both cursor and claude skills to point to that folder.<p>which works except that claude uses .skills&#x2F;synced which is uses to sync changes to skills from claude servers into the skills folder.<p>every other agent I have used just directly syncs into .skills so it ends up duplicating skills","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"0m13","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:52:11.000Z","created_at_i":1790167931,"id":49815320,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"can i ask claude to change these settings for me, and will it enable telemetry as implied checkpoint when i ask it to enable AGENTS.md?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"rvz","children":[{"author":"pbasista","children":[{"author":"wccrawford","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:27:12.000Z","created_at_i":1790170032,"id":49815799,"options":[],"parent_id":49815723,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s not open source.  It&#x27;s more &quot;source available&quot;, since it&#x27;s published, but you legally can&#x27;t do anything with it.  Other than maybe build it yourself, for yourself, I guess.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"SyneRyder","children":[{"author":"pbasista","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:44:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790174680,"id":49816970,"options":[],"parent_id":49816513,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I think you are not missing anything. I have not checked the code itself originally, I am sorry for that. But you are right that there seem to be no actual code for the harness itself. Just the code for (some) mods, plugins and scripts.<p>I just read the first line in the README file which says:<p>&gt; Claude Code is an agentic coding tool ...<p>and I immediately assumed that this is what this repository hosts.<p>It claims that it <i>includes</i> plugins but that does not mean it does not include anything else. It also never explicitly claims, as far as I can tell, that it <i>does not</i> hold the source code of Claude Code, the harness, itself.<p>It is all extremely misleading, in my opinion. Which might be on purpose, unfortunately.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:13:20.000Z","created_at_i":1790172800,"id":49816513,"options":[],"parent_id":49815723,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Forgive me if I&#x27;m missing something really obvious, we&#x27;ll blame it on lack of sleep... but <i>is</i> that actually the full source to Claude Code? I&#x27;m looking at the repository and I only see source for plugins, mods and scripts. When I get to the readme, it says:<p><i>&quot;This repository includes several Claude Code plugins that extend functionality with custom commands and agents. See the plugins directory for detailed documentation on available plugins.&quot;</i><p>But I&#x27;m not a TypeScript guy, so I concede I might be missing something incredibly obvious. I remember there was a leak of the Claude Code source code at one point, and people vibe coding conversions to other languages from the leak, but I don&#x27;t think the Claude Code harness itself is open source or even source available.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"sunaookami","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:16:20.000Z","created_at_i":1790172980,"id":49816558,"options":[],"parent_id":49815723,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"That&#x27;s not the source code. Claude Code is proprietary.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:23:08.000Z","created_at_i":1790169788,"id":49815723,"options":[],"parent_id":49815333,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I understand the motivation for such a concern. But Claude Code in particular has its source code available on GitHub [0].<p>So I am unsure if it is fitting to call it a &quot;closed source&quot; harness.<p>[0] <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code</a><p>Edit: The linked repository does <i>not</i> contain source code for Claude Code, the harness, itself. It only contains the source code for (some) scripts, mods and plugins.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:53:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790167997,"id":49815333,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I am once again (for the third time) [0] asking you to stop using a closed-source harness.<p>[0] <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49760449\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49760449</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"teekert","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:55:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790168102,"id":49815353,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Uhm I turned off everything there is to turn off in my Pro plan, and Claude just read my agents.md with no issue? So... What telemetry am I missing? Or did they JUST update? (I updated my docker image 40 minutes ago to get Opus 5.5, am on version 2.1.280, so not the mentioned 2.1.277, so it&#x27;s fixed?)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mpoteat","children":[{"author":"piltdownman","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:57:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790168244,"id":49815372,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Much respect for the prompt response, humility, and frank disclosure.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"ndbe","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:00:48.000Z","created_at_i":1790168448,"id":49815418,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I don&#x27;t understand, isn&#x27;t coding solved already?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mpoteat","children":[{"author":"rickette","children":[{"author":"oblio","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:17:44.000Z","created_at_i":1790169464,"id":49815648,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"One line change? Pffft. That means you&#x27;re still looking at the code, you&#x27;re behind the times.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"locknitpicker","children":[{"author":"BowBun","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:23:11.000Z","created_at_i":1790169791,"id":49815724,"options":[],"parent_id":49815683,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I think you&#x27;re giving these files too much credit. There are no specs, they are freeform text. In this sense they are the same. The expectation of what could be in it by each vendor means nothing unless it&#x27;s enforced.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"ljm","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:23:21.000Z","created_at_i":1790169801,"id":49815728,"options":[],"parent_id":49815683,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s not a format though is it? it&#x27;s literally just an extension to the system prompt in plain markdown.<p>There is no rhyme or reason to the structure of this file, just like with most things in AI. It&#x27;s best effort human language.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"logifail","children":[{"author":"taormina","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:37:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790170650,"id":49815974,"options":[],"parent_id":49815795,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"No, they do not.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Diti","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:05:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790175924,"id":49817283,"options":[],"parent_id":49815795,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Nope! Claude is even able to understand AsciiDoc just fine (which is a blessing). But it will always insist on the Markdown extension.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:26:49.000Z","created_at_i":1790170009,"id":49815795,"options":[],"parent_id":49815683,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; The document format in CLAUDE.md is whatever Anthropic specifies<p>Q: Do Anthropic actually specify a document format?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"sunaookami","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:14:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790172879,"id":49816538,"options":[],"parent_id":49815683,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"There is no &quot;specification&quot;, it&#x27;s literally just a text file that gets loaded into context. You don&#x27;t even need to write markdown. It&#x27;s not that hard man.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:20:41.000Z","created_at_i":1790169641,"id":49815683,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; The only difference between CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md is the filename. Do you really need a whole plugin system to support that use case? Feels like this could have been a one line change.<p>I don&#x27;t think this is a reasonable assumption. The document format in CLAUDE.md is whatever Anthropic specifies, where AGENTS.md is a common ground format that is expected to be supported by any agent, be it from Anthropic or not.<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;agents.md&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;agents.md&#x2F;</a><p>You might argue that differences are small or negligible, but that is just an expectation.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"stingraycharles","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:23:20.000Z","created_at_i":1790169800,"id":49815727,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Yes, but at the same time, it\u2019s also a good, simple use case to test a new plugin system. I can totally understand that.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"xandrius","children":[{"author":"doublerabbit","children":[{"author":"Anonyneko","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:07:32.000Z","created_at_i":1790172452,"id":49816428,"options":[],"parent_id":49815923,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;youtu.be&#x2F;-AwCEM5K-Ec\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;youtu.be&#x2F;-AwCEM5K-Ec</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:34:29.000Z","created_at_i":1790170469,"id":49815923,"options":[],"parent_id":49815807,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"You sound like my type. hey,  wanna come over to myspace so I could twitter your yahoo till you google all over my facebook?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"newsoftheday","children":[{"author":"ffsm8","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:20:51.000Z","created_at_i":1790176851,"id":49817492,"options":[],"parent_id":49817105,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"<i>Unc you&#x27;re so cooked it&#x27;s not even funny  younger than me but you&#x27;re out here aura farming in the negatives fr fr. NPC-ahh behavior, 0 aura, -1000 rizz. Couldn&#x27;t be me</i><p>Sorry couldn&#x27;t resist (  \uff65\u0e31 \ufe4f \uff65\u0e31 )<p>Not sure what you didn&#x27;t understood in their comment though, maybe the raph loop (and jev which was just released)? Isn&#x27;t the rest completely self explanatory?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"NicoJuicy","children":[{"author":"newsoftheday","children":[{"author":"crooked-v","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:19:53.000Z","created_at_i":1790191193,"id":49821137,"options":[],"parent_id":49820154,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The tl;dr of the tl;dr is treating the model setup like an autonomous robot with its own machine to use and just telling it what to do via chat rather than directly supervising it, which is bonkers in some ways (all the open internet&#x2F;service access&#x2F;permissions stuff you would imagine), and smart in others (a fully isolated machine means it can fuck up something locally or run high-load tests without taking down your important systems).","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"qmanchu","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-25T03:30:37.000Z","created_at_i":1790307037,"id":49839892,"options":[],"parent_id":49820154,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&quot;which was used in the 1800&#x27;s but found their website&quot;<p>The FIRST website, nice.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:08:11.000Z","created_at_i":1790186891,"id":49820154,"options":[],"parent_id":49817755,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"OK I do use AI in the browser but haven&#x27;t tried anything like what you describe. I Googled telegram in case it wasn&#x27;t what I was thinking, which was used in the 1800&#x27;s but found their website. It&#x27;s apparently another messaging platform. Thanks for the interesting view.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"imtringued","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T08:29:28.000Z","created_at_i":1790238568,"id":49827852,"options":[],"parent_id":49817755,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt;some contradiction with Openrouter though<p>No the joke is that you need to protect the review server from a runaway humanoid robot pulling the plug on the review server.<p>Or the opposite, the runaway humanoid robot is controlled by an openclaw server that can&#x27;t be located and shut down.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:38:29.000Z","created_at_i":1790177909,"id":49817755,"options":[],"parent_id":49817105,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s almost all related to LLM&#x27;s, which is fairly new.<p>Basically he&#x27;s describing an LLM assistant setup that does coding on a vps or Mac mini ( some contradiction with Openrouter though) where you can communicate with the assistant through telegram","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Silagi","children":[{"author":"imtringued","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T08:27:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790238460,"id":49827840,"options":[],"parent_id":49820469,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I hate that I understood the post.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790188455,"id":49820469,"options":[],"parent_id":49817105,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I felt a little panic when I understood every word of what was meant to be adjacent to scifi-style garbled engineering speak, and I think I&#x27;d rather be on your side of the spectrum.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:53:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790175204,"id":49817105,"options":[],"parent_id":49815807,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Not related but I think I finally know how it must have felt to the generation prior to mine, when we tried to explain computers to them; because even as a retired 30 year plus software engineer, I have no idea what the comment says.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:27:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790170059,"id":49815807,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Don&#x27;t you run bizantine ralph loops on remote environments with codex security checks, coupled with jev, grok, open router and a fully independent openclaw (on a maxed out mac mini inside a caveau in an undisclosed location, with open telegram) to change constants? You&#x27;re going to be left behind.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"pdpi","children":[{"author":"redox99","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"lunar_mycroft","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"bakugo","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:22:36.000Z","created_at_i":1790180556,"id":49818448,"options":[],"parent_id":49817284,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"At some point, the catering is not worth the sacrifices and future gotchas you&#x27;re going to embed in the code.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"bakugo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:06:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790183215,"id":49819239,"options":[],"parent_id":49817284,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"There&#x27;s no surprising behaviors in that situation. Someone who is aware of the change would most likely delete CLAUDE.md. Someone who is unaware of the change would assume CLAUDE.md is still the one being read by CC, which would hold true.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:05:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790175925,"id":49817284,"options":[],"parent_id":49816669,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Which order do you prefer them in? Since CLAUDE.md is no longer necessary, but was for so long, what happens when users only update AGENTS.md going forward while keeping a stale, unchanged CLAUDE.md around?<p>We&#x27;re talking about changing default behaviors here in ways that can be surprising to users. It&#x27;s reasonable to try and accommodate existing setups, future setups, and - yes - careless users.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:23:44.000Z","created_at_i":1790173424,"id":49816669,"options":[],"parent_id":49816608,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Read CLAUDE.md if it doesn&#x27;t exist read AGENTS.md<p>&gt; Some people might have a different CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md<p>How exactly do these two conflict? If you have both, nothing changes.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dylan604","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"dylan604","children":[{"author":"cgriswald","children":[{"author":"troupo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:21:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790191287,"id":49821163,"options":[],"parent_id":49818473,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Anthropic has the most information and made the choice they made.<p>Anthropic is the last company I would trust to make any decisions. Look at any discussions surrounding their &quot;Claude is a tiny game engine&quot; idiocy, numerous bugs that a junior can discover, a full &quot;plugin system&quot; in which they neeeed a dozen files in the worst Clean Code manner to read one of two files etc.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:23:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790180635,"id":49818473,"options":[],"parent_id":49817965,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This conversation comes down to people saying \u201cWhy don\u2019t you just\u2026\u201d to Anthropic. Anthropic has the most information and made the choice they made. That choice may have been over-engineering, an appropriate choice or both. Discussing that choice <i>could</i> be interesting and it could especially be informative to people without much experience. Speculating on that <i>could</i> lead to an interesting conversation\u2014especially WRT how people are actually using the current status quo\u2014but imagination seems to be lacking here.<p>Instead we get the implicated assertion that users\u2019 existing workflows shouldn\u2019t matter to Anthropic and accusations that someone you don\u2019t agree with is a shill. When called on that you avoided the question.<p>To answer your question, although it wasn\u2019t directed at me: YES. I want people to be able to discuss <i>that exact issue</i> even if it isn\u2019t personally interesting to me.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:52:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790178735,"id":49817965,"options":[],"parent_id":49817255,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Is the level of HN discourse suggesting that having a large number of users worth of never making simple changes something you want? This isn&#x27;t a move fast break things suggestion, this is a rational common sense suggestion. Instead, you&#x27;re pushing an overly complex way of implementing something that would allow for all sorts of unknowns. Earlier comments suggesting this new mods concept was being worked on giving the dev a new 20lb sledge hammer so the CLAUDE&#x2F;AGENTS situation suddenly got beat on like it was a railroad spike when it just needed a smaller hammer since it was only a finishing nail.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:03:33.000Z","created_at_i":1790175813,"id":49817255,"options":[],"parent_id":49816742,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Is accusing someone of &quot;shilling for Anthropic&quot; for suggesting that a bug fix might not be so simple <i>really</i> the level of discourse HN has devolved to now? Is it the kind of HN <i>you</i> want?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:27:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790173677,"id":49816742,"options":[],"parent_id":49816608,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"if [ !-f CLAUDE.md ]; then \n  AGENTS.md\nfi<p>you&#x27;re really over thinking this, and i&#x27;m wondering if you&#x27;re risking pulling something stretching like that to pick this up shilling for Anthropic.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"lunar_mycroft","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"lunar_mycroft","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:33:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790181210,"id":49818667,"options":[],"parent_id":49817582,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I see, well I&#x27;m not particularly concerned with being right on this topic (call it a difference of opinion or matter of taste), so I wish you a pleasant day.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:27:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790177230,"id":49817582,"options":[],"parent_id":49817309,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"We&#x27;ve had a long discussion only because <i>you</i> refuse to admit that a very simple solution would work (despite completely failing to show how it wouldn&#x27;t).  The problem is that your opinion is not in fact proof that you&#x27;re right.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:07:05.000Z","created_at_i":1790176025,"id":49817309,"options":[],"parent_id":49816744,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Okay, so we agree that this fix isn&#x27;t <i>quite</i> as simple as it sounds then, yes? We&#x27;ve just had 3+ paragraphs of discussion around potential edge cases and additional considerations beyond &quot;read one of two files.&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:28:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790173682,"id":49816744,"options":[],"parent_id":49816608,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"First, GP&#x27;s proposal already addresses that.  If both are present, CLAUDE.md would be used.  Second, that is solved with a settings toggle.  Read a boolean from .claude&#x2F;settings.json and disable the new behavior if it&#x27;s true (or false, depending on what you want to name the setting).  third, you skipped the second part of my question: &quot;how would implementing it the way Anthropic did address that?&quot;  Implementing the same behavior through multiple layers of abstraction and an order of magnitude more code doesn&#x27;t solve the issue you mentioned.<p>Bonus forth point: why is this critical to solve for claude code, but not for all the <i>other</i> harnesses which have all converged on AGENTS.md for this purpose?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:19:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790173180,"id":49816608,"options":[],"parent_id":49816562,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Some people might have a different CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md because they use Claude to do one thing and $other_agent to do another thing. Or because Claude does XYZ by default, and other agents do ABC, and they want to give the correct guidance to both.<p>This is, to me, a completely reasonable and believable use case that could break if you implement this fix without &quot;overengineering&quot; it.<p>A setting to disable what? Be specific. See? Not so simple...","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:16:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790172994,"id":49816562,"options":[],"parent_id":49816457,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"How, exactly, would the proposed solution (combined with a setting to disable it) break, and how would implementing it the way Anthropic did address that?  Be specific.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dylan604","children":[{"author":"troupo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:22:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790191378,"id":49821186,"options":[],"parent_id":49816699,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Strange then that Anthropic answers to all user issues with complete derision","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:25:28.000Z","created_at_i":1790173528,"id":49816699,"options":[],"parent_id":49816457,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I&#x27;ve never heard of the &#x27;move fast, break things&#x27; mentality ever giving a damn about number of users. If so, no changes would ever be made. The great thing about having millions of users is QA can be eliminated entirely as you&#x27;ll start hearing about issues from the users directly.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"amluto","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:09:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790176142,"id":49817338,"options":[],"parent_id":49816826,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"What&#x27;s your point? Nobody can hold themselves to a higher standard because they didn&#x27;t in the past?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:34:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790174086,"id":49816826,"options":[],"parent_id":49816457,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Frontier lab AI agent tools break their users\u2019 workflows worse than this on a regular basis.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dotancohen","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:18:14.000Z","created_at_i":1790176694,"id":49817463,"options":[],"parent_id":49816457,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Bash does this well, reading only the first of half a dozen config file locations it searches. And if the user needs it to read from an additional location, just add a source line to that location.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"0x457","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:01:06.000Z","created_at_i":1790208066,"id":49824404,"options":[],"parent_id":49816457,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; This line of thinking is something you will quickly be disabused of once you try supporting software that hundreds of millions of people use.<p>&gt; And I say this as someone that loves the Unix philosophy dearly.<p>Unix way would be just to tell users to `ln -s` and stop bothering with this.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:09:23.000Z","created_at_i":1790172563,"id":49816457,"options":[],"parent_id":49816174,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This line of thinking is something you will quickly be disabused of once you try supporting software that hundreds of millions of people use.<p>And I say this as someone that loves the Unix philosophy dearly.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:50:01.000Z","created_at_i":1790171401,"id":49816174,"options":[],"parent_id":49816061,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"That line of thought is the reason why everything gets so overengineered.<p>Read CLAUDE.md if it doesn&#x27;t exist read AGENTS.md you don&#x27;t need to overthink it so much.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"epihelix","children":[{"author":"vikramkr","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:36:38.000Z","created_at_i":1790174198,"id":49816860,"options":[],"parent_id":49816561,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Because when you have tons of users ainor fuckuo is a big fuckup and also it&#x27;s really common to have both claude.md and agents.md and use @ syntax (which lets you reference markdown files when using Claude code, but not other harnesses) so you Claude md looks like<p>```md\n@AGENTS.md<p>[Claude specific stuff]<p>```<p>And then what happens if someone now puts @syntax in their agents.md triggering a loop etc. It&#x27;s all vibe coded - including code from days with dumber models - there&#x27;s gonna be all sorts of dragons under the hood","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"hamburglar","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:07:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790176078,"id":49817326,"options":[],"parent_id":49816561,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; What, exactly, is going to go horribly wrong here ...?<p>Operating anything at scale teaches you that the universe of \u201cthings that can go horribly wrong\u201d has a much better imagination than you.  That goes quadruple with complex and squishy reasoning models.<p>I\u2019ve seen a couple of really good examples of what can go wrong in this subthread, the most straightforward of which is that abruptly changing a fundamental behavior can break existing use cases.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:16:33.000Z","created_at_i":1790172993,"id":49816561,"options":[],"parent_id":49816061,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Having a kill switch for the change is a perfectly reasonable safety measure in case something goes horribly wrong.<p>What, exactly, is going to go horribly wrong here ...?  The worst case you&#x27;re proposing is that an Anthropic model acts on AGENTS.md rather than CLAUDE.md.  It&#x27;s not going to be the end of the world; at worst it&#x27;ll be `git reset --hard HEAD` time.  But this wouldn&#x27;t happen, because:<p>&gt; The correct behaviour in the presence of both files is not obvious, either.<p>It seems extremely obvious to me: the non-breaking change is the right change here.  If both exist, Anthropic models continue to use CLAUDE.md and ignore AGENTS.md.  This is not rocket science.  Why are we overthinking this?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Wowfunhappy","children":[{"author":"californical","children":[{"author":"dotancohen","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:15:54.000Z","created_at_i":1790176554,"id":49817425,"options":[],"parent_id":49817186,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I would like to subscribe to your newsletter.<p>Seriously, though, this is a great idea. Good communicators know to tailor their discourse to their audience. LLMs are just as sensitive to small variations in prompts, and just as inconsistent between them, as are humans.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Wowfunhappy","children":[{"author":"markhahn","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:52:19.000Z","created_at_i":1790178739,"id":49817966,"options":[],"parent_id":49817593,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"careful, that might lead to programming.  using, you know, a programming language.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"californical","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:30:50.000Z","created_at_i":1790181050,"id":49818608,"options":[],"parent_id":49817593,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Sorry how about this:<p><pre><code>    # Models.Claude\\*:\n</code></pre>\nMaybe now it can be in a .md again :D","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:27:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790177254,"id":49817593,"options":[],"parent_id":49817186,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s not a bad idea, although at that point it probably shouldn&#x27;t be a .md file anymore. You&#x27;d want to use YAML or something.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"everforward","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:38:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790177907,"id":49817754,"options":[],"parent_id":49817186,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I did this at one point with Jinja templates.<p>I wrote an agent launcher sort of bash script. Pass in the command to start the agent, the script checks if there\u2019s a Jinja file in a special directory matching that name, and builds it to AGENTS.md. Then it launches the agent.<p>I was trying to use it as a sort of janky RAG. I had a bunch of snippets (one for DB architecture, one for how load balancing works, etc), and my Jinja files were mostly a list of snippets to pull in. Voila, a bunch of agents that share little pieces of info but have a single source of truth.<p>I never got a ton of value tbh, it was very good at just grepping the snippets.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:59:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790175580,"id":49817186,"options":[],"parent_id":49816610,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Within agents.md, an idea. Feel free to steal if you work on this:<p><pre><code>    Model.Claude*:\n      Do this one thing\n\n    Model.Claude.Opus.4.8:\n      Extra specific instructions\n\n    Model.*:\n      This is relevant to everyone\n\n    Harness.ClaudeCode*:\n      Why not, let\u2019s allow harness specific instructions so you can do things differently depending how you\u2019re working</code></pre>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:19:51.000Z","created_at_i":1790173191,"id":49816610,"options":[],"parent_id":49816061,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; somebody, somewhere, was taking advantage of that to give one set of instructions to Claude, and a different set of instructions to some other provider.<p>I&#x27;m this person, I am actively doing this! I have some instructions which the Claude models need and OpenAI models will do by themselves. If the OpenAI models see the Claude instructions, they will go way overboard in a way I don&#x27;t want.<p>Mind, the change does not affect me at all, because when  both instructions are present Claude continues to read CLAUDE.md and Codex continues to read AGENTS.md. But if Claude started preferring AGENTS.md, that would be mildly annoying.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"bakugo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:22:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790173322,"id":49816646,"options":[],"parent_id":49816061,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This &quot;tiny feature&quot; consists of hundreds of lines of code spread across 57 source files, many of which are less than 30 lines long, often contain more comments than code, and have no real reason to exist. It&#x27;s the very definition of overengineering and overcomplexity.<p>That said, I do find it somewhat funny that Anthropic themselves are falling victim to their own model&#x27;s tokenmaxxing.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"speleding","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:31:42.000Z","created_at_i":1790173902,"id":49816788,"options":[],"parent_id":49816061,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The Claude sandbox has a slightly different ENV compared to ChatGPT (LC_CTYPE set to C instead of UTF8 I believe) which upsets some scripts we have.<p>So in the CLAUDE.MD we tell it about that and then tell it continue reading AGENTS.MD. Not very hard to work around if CLAUDE.MD goes away, but just to support your point that the split did have its uses for some.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dotancohen","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:13:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790176382,"id":49817391,"options":[],"parent_id":49816061,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"<p><pre><code>  &gt; Having a kill switch for the change is a perfectly reasonable safety measure in case something goes horribly wrong.\n</code></pre>\nHaving a way for the user to revert the update is a perfectly reasonable safety measure in case something goes horribly wrong.<p>Even though Anthropic or any other software provider could technically run anything on our system, there exists a modicum of trust between supplier and user. Anthropic performing arbitrary changes <i>that are tangential but not specific to the premise of delivering a harness to package code files and prompts in context to their LLM</i> breaks that trust for many users.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:43:05.000Z","created_at_i":1790170985,"id":49816061,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The plugin system itself was probably already in the making, and they just chose to implement this tiny feature as a plugin to try it out.<p>As for the only difference being the file name, that&#x27;s an untested assumption. Up until now, Claude hadn&#x27;t supported AGENTS.md, and it&#x27;s a simple application of Hyrum&#x27;s Law that somebody, somewhere, was taking advantage of that to give one set of instructions to Claude, and a different set of instructions to some other provider. The correct behaviour in the presence of <i>both</i> files is not obvious, either.<p>Having a kill switch for the change is a perfectly reasonable safety measure in case something goes horribly wrong.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"chrisweekly","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:56:22.000Z","created_at_i":1790171782,"id":49816258,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"With apologies for not just testing this myself (currently AFK), doesn&#x27;t it still work to have a CLAUDE.md file containing just `@AGENTS.md`?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"chrisjj","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:10:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790172625,"id":49816470,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Do you really need a whole plugin system<p>Vibe-coding gotta vibe-code.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"bakugo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:13:09.000Z","created_at_i":1790172789,"id":49816509,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Go download the leaked source code from earlier this year, search for all occurrences of the string `CLAUDE.md`, and be horrified.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"flippingheck","children":[{"author":"dotancohen","children":[{"author":"dotancohen","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T21:59:09.000Z","created_at_i":1790287149,"id":49837261,"options":[],"parent_id":49817521,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"To the guy who asked but his comment is dead:<p><pre><code>  &gt; Are you gating by license or user, or just by percentage of installs?\n</code></pre>\nI&#x27;m gating by version. I want to dogfood features personally before releasing them to all my users.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:22:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790176975,"id":49817521,"options":[],"parent_id":49816679,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I&#x27;d love to hear more about this. Though I usually write bespoke software for specific clients, I&#x27;m about to release my first general-availability application. It&#x27;s a rust application with Python GUI on the desktop (Linux, Mac, Windows) and a skinny Android application that wraps the rust on mobile. I&#x27;m going to be gating features starting probably next week. I&#x27;d love to hear tips and experience for implementing feature flags, for both the desktop and mobile space.<p>Thanks!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:24:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790173450,"id":49816679,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"At $FAANG, ~all changes go through feature flags.<p>There are processes to make changes outside of feature flags, but they have enough friction that it&#x27;s easier to just use a feature flag.<p>This level of paranoia is consistent with the blast radius of changes breaking Claude users.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"rmnclmnt","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:56:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790175387,"id":49817140,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Welcome to SWE in 2026","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"verdverm","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:09:14.000Z","created_at_i":1790176154,"id":49817341,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"need to, no, but if you put the Ai to task, expect over engineering","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"wldcordeiro","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:14:06.000Z","created_at_i":1790180046,"id":49818316,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"We&#x27;ve just had a file called `.rules` that is symlink as `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, etc to support the 3 or so common ones used around our projects.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"sebmellen","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:05:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790186757,"id":49820121,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I always point people back to <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;grugbrain.dev\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;grugbrain.dev</a>.<p>The worst thing about AI is endless complexity slopification.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"pasteleft","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:02:49.000Z","created_at_i":1790190169,"id":49820898,"options":[],"parent_id":49815527,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I&#x27;m not sure why they didn&#x27;t just extend plugins, but having mod support is definitely a plus for everyone.<p>AGENTS.md seems to simply showcase what mods are capable of.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:09:00.000Z","created_at_i":1790168940,"id":49815527,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The only difference between CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md is the filename. Do you really need a whole plugin system to support that use case? Feels like this could have been a one line change.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"d5lt5","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:25:14.000Z","created_at_i":1790169914,"id":49815760,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Sounds like you&#x27;ve read the deepseek harness paper.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dybber","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:05:09.000Z","created_at_i":1790172309,"id":49816387,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Will you extend your plugin to read skills and rules from `.agents`? Or should we write our own plugin&#x2F;mod for that?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"amluto","children":[{"author":"kaszanka","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:47:22.000Z","created_at_i":1790174842,"id":49817023,"options":[],"parent_id":49816799,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"If the direct link isn&#x27;t working for anyone else (looks like it&#x27;s some AWS pre-signed one maybe tied to IP): <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;user-attachments&#x2F;files&#x2F;31802150&#x2F;EXTERNAL.Function.Hooks.Core.Architecture.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;user-attachments&#x2F;files&#x2F;31802150&#x2F;EXTERNAL....</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dogleash","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:12:18.000Z","created_at_i":1790176338,"id":49817383,"options":[],"parent_id":49816799,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; they are noun phrases and not sentences at all? I\u2019m pretty sure that any decent pre-LLM NLP-based grammar checker would correctly flag half the sentences in Claudish.  Also, whatever variant of Claude wrote this thing can\u2019t even capitalize around semicolons consistently with itself, let alone consistently with how English has been written for at least a century.<p>Probably just a case of a company hoping their scale can change the societal standard faster than they can be bothered to match the standard.<p>You&#x27;ll talk like 2023 unsupervised TikTok generators and you&#x27;ll be happy.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mpoteat","children":[{"author":"amluto","children":[{"author":"amluto","children":[{"author":"hluska","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T01:37:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790213822,"id":49825118,"options":[],"parent_id":49820584,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"For someone so pedantic, your writing is remarkably poor.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:42:38.000Z","created_at_i":1790188958,"id":49820584,"options":[],"parent_id":49817532,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Having given the JSON more than two seconds of thought, I have a very different suggestion:<p><pre><code>    {\n     &quot;function_hooks&quot;: {\n      &quot;version&quot;: 1,\n      &quot;source_file&quot;: &quot;.&#x2F;whatever.ts&quot;,\n      &quot;language&quot;: &quot;TypeScript&quot;,\n      &quot;hash&quot;: &quot;sha256:abcd...&quot;\n     }\n    }\n</code></pre>\nDon&#x27;t trust my formatting -- I typed this in the comment box and I have not run it through a prettifier or anything.<p>The point here is that there&#x27;s a world adjacent to but not actually contained within Claude Code in which not everything blindly trusts everything else, and maybe it&#x27;s time to start remembering some lessons from the 90&#x27;s on.  For example:<p>- Don&#x27;t sniff content types and preferably don&#x27;t infer them from filenames either.<p>- Don&#x27;t trust your subresource to arrive intact.  Pin those hashes and verify them!<p>- Leave some room for extensibility.<p>- Maybe don&#x27;t require everyone to mix their code with the security policy that controls edits to that code?  I realize that anyone cursed with GitHub Actions is forced to violate this rule in the most outrageous ways imaginable, but that doesn&#x27;t mean that Claude Code needs to follow suit forever.  Once there&#x27;s subresource integrity, the actual subresource can be put <i>somewhere else</i> where it belongs better.  If there&#x27;s &quot;source_file&quot;, in the future there can be &quot;source_url&quot; and such without trying to infer it from the formatting of the string.<p>(I&#x27;ve involved absolutely no AI in the preparation of this comment.  I make plenty of use of AI, but I like my brain to stay exercised, and I like to think that I remain MUCH better at this kind of thing than even the best current models.)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:23:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790177014,"id":49817532,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Your comment here is written in perfectly fine English :)<p>Maybe &quot;function_hook_modules&quot; for the JSON key?<p>Does this finally fix the limitation that there is no supportable way to <i>replace</i> the implementation of a native tool in Claude Code?  codex-rs has an (undocumented but likely supportable if kind of awkward) mechanism, and I\u2019m part way through a project that needs this. I was going to release it with a recommendation not to use Claude Code, but it\u2019s at least plausible that this will change my mind.  (I\u2019m not sure yet \u2014 the $ mechanism might be too restrictive.  It\u2019s a start at least.)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"xena","children":[{"author":"mpoteat","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:40:50.000Z","created_at_i":1790178050,"id":49817789,"options":[],"parent_id":49817589,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Wow, you&#x27;re Xe Iaso! I&#x27;ve reached out.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:27:26.000Z","created_at_i":1790177246,"id":49817589,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Contact me at the email address in my HN account and we can arrange for a human with a soul and feelings to write the docs from scratch assuming you have a price in mind that values the nature of my talent and experience.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"massagedpelican","children":[{"author":"KurtMueller","children":[{"author":"sebmellen","children":[{"author":"computomatic","children":[{"author":"sebmellen","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T02:18:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790216297,"id":49825406,"options":[],"parent_id":49823535,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Well, I&#x27;ve tried to get around it for our corporate SEO blogging strategy, and I&#x27;ve found that it&#x27;s just not possible to do it (even with really crazy techniques where you have different models combined to produce the output, or you change your prompting style massively). The minute I take the same article that the LLM gave me and I rewrite it in my own voice (meaning just take the information and topics, but rewrite it from scratch), the post works immediately and passes as 100% human on Pangram.<p>The only thing that gets around that is StealthGPT, but it mangles your intent in the output so badly that it&#x27;s easier to just write the thing yourself.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T22:34:56.000Z","created_at_i":1790202896,"id":49823535,"options":[],"parent_id":49820078,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"How do you evaluate that?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:03:04.000Z","created_at_i":1790186584,"id":49820078,"options":[],"parent_id":49819704,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"There\u2019s definitely a snake oil component, but Pangram is unbelievably accurate. Creepily so in my opinion","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:37:11.000Z","created_at_i":1790185031,"id":49819704,"options":[],"parent_id":49818689,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Perhaps these &quot;ai detectors&quot; are snake oil","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"karagenit","children":[{"author":"echoangle","children":[{"author":"thinkingemote","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T20:15:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790194540,"id":49821869,"options":[],"parent_id":49820987,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I know it&#x27;s a joke but if you look at many of the key AI researchers papers (written pre-LLM mass adoption) you can see some similarities with how LLMs structure their output.<p>I&#x27;d love to do some stylometry on this...","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:08:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790190519,"id":49820987,"options":[],"parent_id":49820597,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Maybe Claude is RLHFd primarily on texts by mpoteat and that\u2019s why it talks this way","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"bmitc","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:43:23.000Z","created_at_i":1790210603,"id":49824695,"options":[],"parent_id":49820597,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I have found that Opus 5 and Fable love bringing up category theory at the drop of a hat.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:43:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790189007,"id":49820597,"options":[],"parent_id":49818689,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Yeah, this doc is really interesting. It has some absolutely claude-fried lines like:<p>&gt; A hook is Koa-style middleware: it reifies an endomorphic continuation<p>&gt; Five forms, each on tool.call;<p>But on the other hand uses distinctly human phrases like \u201cone may\u201d and \u201cetc.&#x2F;e.g.\u201d that I rarely see LLMs use. Not sure what to think.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:34:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790181270,"id":49818689,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Out of curiosity, I ran the PDF through pangram and it seemed to flag nearly the entire thing as AI. I recognize these aren&#x27;t perfect detectors, but they can give signals if nothing else. Perhaps it needs more soul injected!<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.pangram.com&#x2F;history&#x2F;93f9ec71-f7b3-4680-86b1-ff129549cb16?ucc=VlhV1svqmKk\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.pangram.com&#x2F;history&#x2F;93f9ec71-f7b3-4680-86b1-ff12...</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"arbot360","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:44:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790185442,"id":49819796,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Not beating the allegations on &quot;Claude doesn&#x27;t speak human because Anthropic employees don&#x27;t speak human.&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"SupLockDef","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:27:01.000Z","created_at_i":1790191621,"id":49821235,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I am going to be called on that one, but I have to call on your bullshit here. You didn&#x27;t write this.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"crooked-v","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T20:04:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790193897,"id":49821734,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s a register that would be great for some tabletop games or pop science writing, but in this context it could really use a technical editor to aggressively remove phrasing like &quot;keeping the fold neatly uniform&quot; and &quot;affordance surface&quot;, as well as change things like &quot;hooks live in a hooks.json file, today of four extant types&quot; into plain technical language (&quot;there are four types of hook that can be defined in hooks.json&quot;).","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"ipsi","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T20:42:35.000Z","created_at_i":1790196155,"id":49822276,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Ouch! Much of this verbiage was dictated by me personally; I just have a fairly distinct register some might consider inscrutable.<p>I do notice that the more Claude-generated stuff I read, the more it creeps into my daily usage, and I suspect I don&#x27;t read nearly as much of it as an Anthropic Employee would, so I could believe that. Though &quot;much of&quot; isn&#x27;t the same as &quot;written with zero AI generation&#x2F;rephrasing&#x2F;etc.&quot;<p>Anyway, that aside, something I would like to see is an example of something that&#x27;s possible with this system that isn&#x27;t, or isn&#x27;t <i>easily</i>, possible with existing Claude hooks. Right now it reads like &quot;Here&#x27;s a cool thing! Here&#x27;s how it works! And here&#x27;s this other similar system we have! Here&#x27;s how that works!&quot; But there&#x27;s no summary of the differences, why I&#x27;d use this over regular hooks, and so on. Or at least not that I saw on quick skim, and I&#x27;d be looking for that to be mentioned as early as possible, so I know if the rest is worth reading.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"ApatheticCosmos","children":[{"author":"datadrivenangel","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T23:52:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790207560,"id":49824312,"options":[],"parent_id":49823481,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"her writing style isn&#x27;t normally this claudish though!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"nextaccountic","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T04:13:08.000Z","created_at_i":1790223188,"id":49826174,"options":[],"parent_id":49823481,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Well regardless of the origins of Claude-speak, I&#x27;m sure millions of humans are picking up some of its idioms, and at least some fraction of it will enter standard English in some decades","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T22:29:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790202597,"id":49823481,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"What if we have it all backwards?  What if Claude-speak, as some like to call it, is actually caused by this one dude dictating the documentation?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"hluska","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T01:35:22.000Z","created_at_i":1790213722,"id":49825105,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Your writing is fine, documentation is hard and nobody is perfect at launch. I can all but guarantee I have more editing experience than the commenter and trust me, you\u2019re fine.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"iam-TJ","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T14:53:33.000Z","created_at_i":1790261613,"id":49831486,"options":[],"parent_id":49817401,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I think the various recent articles about agent output using ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English are quite pertinent here. For example:<p>&quot;Agent Skill to Force Docs in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English&quot;<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49114639\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49114639</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:14:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790176453,"id":49817401,"options":[],"parent_id":49816799,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Ouch! Much of this verbiage was dictated by me personally; I just have a fairly distinct register some might consider inscrutable. My English teachers in grade school always said the same :)<p>Rest assured I&#x27;ll inject a bit less soul into the official docs once Mods are launched; re your feedback on the JSON key, what would you recommend?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"JDups","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:52:32.000Z","created_at_i":1790193152,"id":49821569,"options":[],"parent_id":49816799,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Writing documentation is one of the most often mentioned uses of LLMs. I suppose if Anthropic wouldn&#x27;t be doing it it would put into question why anyone else would.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"hluska","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T01:33:38.000Z","created_at_i":1790213618,"id":49825091,"options":[],"parent_id":49816799,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I\u2019m curious\u2026 would you talk to them like this in person? The only \u2018egregious\u2019 thing I read here was your reaction. Maybe you could consider acting more human?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"yearolinuxdsktp","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T02:49:36.000Z","created_at_i":1790218176,"id":49825621,"options":[],"parent_id":49816799,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Here&#x27;s a palatable, clear version:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;pdfhost.io&#x2F;v&#x2F;2CVhPGy9Kw_CLEAR_Function_Hooks_Core_Architecture\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;pdfhost.io&#x2F;v&#x2F;2CVhPGy9Kw_CLEAR_Function_Hooks_Core_Ar...</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:33:00.000Z","created_at_i":1790173980,"id":49816799,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I skimmed a couple pages of the docs at:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;user-attachments&#x2F;files&#x2F;31802150&#x2F;EXTERNAL.Function.Hooks.Core.Architecture.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;user-attachments&#x2F;files&#x2F;31802150&#x2F;EXTERNAL....</a><p>Might I gently suggest that you have a model at least as capable as Opus 5.5 translate that from Claudish to English?  Or, even better, have an actual human work on the docs a bit?  As it stands, they are fairly egregious, and they seem to devote at least as much space to little AI-generated quips that convey no meaning than to actually explaining what\u2019s going on.<p>Also, maybe a human should decide whether these are \u201cfunction\u201d hooks or \u201cmodule\u201d hooks. All of this marketing calls them \u201cfunction\u201d hooks, but the json config seems entirely unaware of this.<p>(Has anyone else noticed that half the sentences in Claudish aren\u2019t merely weird: they are noun phrases and not sentences at all?  I\u2019m pretty sure that any decent pre-LLM NLP-based grammar checker would correctly flag half the sentences in Claudish.  Also, whatever variant of Claude wrote this thing can\u2019t even capitalize around semicolons consistently with itself, let alone consistently with how English has been written for at least a century.)<p>edit: Fixed the link.  Thanks, kaszanka.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"63stack","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:38:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790174293,"id":49816881,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt;via our new extensibility system for CC, called Mods, which is launching soon-ish. A mod is a plugin with a new type of hook, which we call a function hook.<p>An extensibility system called mods, which is a plugin with a new type of hook that we call function hook?<p>I can&#x27;t tell if this is real, or you are making fun of overengineered AI solutions.<p>Is this real?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"c0rruptbytes","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:19:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790176753,"id":49817473,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"mods seem like a grasp at all the pi and dsh users","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"glub","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:44:52.000Z","created_at_i":1790178292,"id":49817843,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I&#x27;ve developed several plugins for different harnesses, and I needed some upstream change for most of them.<p>The deciding factor for me whether or not I will work on the feature of the plugin is whether I (or rather, my agent) can look in upstream source and evaluate if it can be done with minimal upstream change, which I then contribute. And generally, even if no upstream change is needed, agents work so much better when they can read the code.<p>So why not just make Claude code open source? Considering also that source code was leaked once anyway.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"crooked-v","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:09:07.000Z","created_at_i":1790190547,"id":49820994,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This may or may not be related, but if you&#x27;re working on CC, who do we have to annoy to make Anthropic stop trying to force use of arbitrary Bash commands instead of the actual tool calls built into the harness? (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;issues&#x2F;90450\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;issues&#x2F;90450</a>, <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;issues&#x2F;89251\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;issues&#x2F;89251</a>, etc) It&#x27;s deeply infuriating at times that there&#x27;s this full system of hooks, permissions, etc that&#x27;s unusable at times because CC keeps trying to make the model not use any of it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"troupo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:16:26.000Z","created_at_i":1790190986,"id":49821095,"options":[],"parent_id":49815421,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; The AGENTS.md support was implemented via our new extensibility system for CC, called Mods,<p>AKA &quot;we need 100~ish files wrtitten in the most horrible Clean Code style replete with no two files agreeing on the same naming of the same feature... to read one of two files, one of which has been a de-facto industry standard for over two years&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:01:06.000Z","created_at_i":1790168466,"id":49815421,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The AGENTS.md support was implemented via our new extensibility system for CC, called Mods, which is launching soon-ish. A mod is a plugin with a new type of hook, which we call a function hook.<p>If folks play around with it, I would love feedback on the relevant issue: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;issues&#x2F;91870\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;issues&#x2F;91870</a><p>Mods allow quite a bit more customizability and control. I really believe in the idea.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"michaellee8","children":[{"author":"d5lt5","children":[{"author":"bpodgursky","children":[{"author":"d5lt5","children":[{"author":"bpodgursky","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:09:33.000Z","created_at_i":1790172573,"id":49816458,"options":[],"parent_id":49816427,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Right... you can just do it yourself.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"farlight","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"d5lt5","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[{"author":"d5lt5","children":[{"author":"arcfour","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-26T15:25:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790436339,"id":49857457,"options":[],"parent_id":49828088,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Huh? I like my functional OS? How am I going to submit PRs to fix Windows?<p>Are you alright?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T09:06:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790240777,"id":49828088,"options":[],"parent_id":49817357,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Maybe you can link your PRs where you fixed the system.<p>Or maybe you are just another brainwashed person who decided to follow the flock&#x2F;horde, because OS&#x27;es are not about emotions, but about getting stuff done. If you feel emotional about the tool, I have bad news for you, and good news for your future therapist.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:09:51.000Z","created_at_i":1790176191,"id":49817357,"options":[],"parent_id":49816888,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Yes, I prefer to use functional operating systems, or at least ones I can fix myself, without incurring a &quot;huge performance hit&quot; by wrapping them in spyware disguised as an OS ;-)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:39:01.000Z","created_at_i":1790174341,"id":49816888,"options":[],"parent_id":49816555,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"There is a very valid reason on Windows not to allow people to do &#x27;ln -s&#x27; without an admin.<p>WSL also has a huge perf hit when you cross FS boundary, but perhaps you have never experienced it, because you said, &quot;Ah, right. Windows...&quot;<p>But at least you&#x27;ve heard about WSL!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:16:12.000Z","created_at_i":1790172972,"id":49816555,"options":[],"parent_id":49816545,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Ah, right. Windows...<p>Does that apply to WSL? I would assume everyone develops on WSL these days if they have to use Windows, at least...","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:14:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790172895,"id":49816545,"options":[],"parent_id":49816486,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"On Windows you do. If you have to suffer it for some reason.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:11:12.000Z","created_at_i":1790172672,"id":49816486,"options":[],"parent_id":49816427,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"? You need root to run ln? Since when?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:07:28.000Z","created_at_i":1790172448,"id":49816427,"options":[],"parent_id":49816337,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Symlink requires admin, and most people do not run CC as admin with bypass permissions though.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:02:23.000Z","created_at_i":1790172143,"id":49816337,"options":[],"parent_id":49815693,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This is the most symbolic and unimportant change in history (you can literally just symlink), I think people will be fine.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"vikramkr","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:39:41.000Z","created_at_i":1790174381,"id":49816893,"options":[],"parent_id":49815693,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"There are two or three relevant companies in this space in America and this is the one of them that kicked off the whole terminal agent harness thing in getting market adoption. It&#x27;s perfectly fine for neither of these companies to follow industry standards while they&#x27;re figuring shit out","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:21:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790169670,"id":49815693,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"On the other hand, if Anthropic is to follow the industry standards, this would never have happened in the first place. It&#x27;s not like the feature gates are the frontier of software development.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"BowBun","children":[{"author":"user43928","children":[{"author":"dannyw","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:51:09.000Z","created_at_i":1790185869,"id":49819906,"options":[],"parent_id":49816165,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Don\u2019t make too quick snap judgements. \u201cHoneymooning\u201d, or giving new subscriptions &#x2F; upgrades extra usage or \u201cjuice\u201d is pretty common industry practice amongst SaaS \u201cgrowth hacking\u201d for years. Sadly.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:49:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790171379,"id":49816165,"options":[],"parent_id":49815738,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"After I was mildly disappointed with GPT-6 Sol and Luna not improving intelligence and only cutting the price, I&#x27;m running Opus 5.5 today.<p>After the last month or so in the Codex app, I was pleased with the Claude app.<p>It might be a case of the grass always being greener on the other side, but this is what stands out:<p>After 3-4 hours of usage, the weekly usage limit moved by only 1%.<p>Compared to Astra where I can watch the limit draining live, this is a great improvement.<p>I&#x27;d estimate it 3x cheaper, and that&#x27;s with a 450k context limit instead of the 258k in Codex.<p>So far Opus 5.5 appears less prone to stopping for no apparent reason at checkpoints in the middle of a longer task.<p>It doesn&#x27;t open an internal browser with a useless comparison page, where it then proceeds to add notes despite no one having asked for it.<p>It is a breath of fresh air: I get the response in the chat, while the Codex app recently loves randomly opening artifacts instead.<p>Opus 5.5 xhigh made great progress on the task, more so than Astra High, but that could be random chance.<p>Oh, and the &#x27;Auto&#x27; mode actually works and does not force me to instead run &#x27;Full access&#x27; like in the Codex app, lest it blocks even &#x27;git push&#x27;.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:24:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790169842,"id":49815738,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Because they respond to HN threads about their products? Which are likely Claude hooks monitoring for activity in the first place? Come on...<p>At least make an argument for switching vendors based on the quality or price of their service.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"m3kw9","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:51:01.000Z","created_at_i":1790171461,"id":49816186,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Sure a fast response on HN would make people switch.   Try better rates, infra, limits etc.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"cowboylowrez","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:05:51.000Z","created_at_i":1790172351,"id":49816396,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"What we need is a low level but constant drumbeat against openai in general. In general the AI situation is overleveraged and underpoliced, with the occasional hints of AI gone wild. If openai were to just be left to die, we could let that financial mess unroll and bail out the leftovers, I don&#x27;t like bailouts anymore than the next guy but with this administration its almost a guarantee if things go south because this adminstration can charge administrative fees of maybe $20-30 billion (which goes to trump), get Sam Altman to serve one or two years in a cushy resort type fed place for the hugging face hacking and put openai&#x27;s processes on github as a premium feature, say $10000 a month to access (which again goes to trump).<p>I know I know, why are we giving money to trump? Its because he&#x27;s going to take it anyways so can&#x27;t we at least apply some window dressing?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"jimmaswell","children":[{"author":"enraged_camel","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:43:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790174620,"id":49816954,"options":[],"parent_id":49816843,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Wow, thanks for sharing your experience. Very insightful.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"michaellee8","children":[{"author":"jimmaswell","children":[{"author":"dannyw","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:48:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790185690,"id":49819861,"options":[],"parent_id":49817549,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It\u2019s more likely that GP encountered some bug or corner case or weird experiment conflating than anything intentionally deceptive.<p>There\u2019s also the fact that LLMs aren\u2019t perfect, and sometimes even the best models act really stupid sometimes.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:24:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790177087,"id":49817549,"options":[],"parent_id":49817078,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Somehow this just hasn&#x27;t happened to me. I use Astra on high all day for fairly intensive game dev tasks, sometimes cranked up depending on the task.<p>I have heard ultra thinking might delegate to worse agents for some of its sub-tasks, but I don&#x27;t use that much anymore since Astra came out. Just high seems good enough to throw most laundry lists at.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"nullbio","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:36:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790177785,"id":49817720,"options":[],"parent_id":49817078,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s night and day difference, for 3 days, until Anthropic nerf the model.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"troupo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:28:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790191737,"id":49821257,"options":[],"parent_id":49817078,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Cuz OpenAI has been secretly downgrading models on many accounts, including mine lately.<p>Same with Anthropic. On top of that Anthropic rarely or ever admits any issues, and even if they do, you get like 6 hours of reset. Rmemeber March?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:51:04.000Z","created_at_i":1790175064,"id":49817078,"options":[],"parent_id":49816843,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Cuz OpenAI has been secretly downgrading models on many accounts, including mine lately. I paid $200 a month since like gpt-5.4, and since Astra released I found the model is somehow acting strange, it is until I checked X I have discovered that OAI is giving Luna level models when I am requesting Sol&#x2F;Astra, or some piece of s** that is even worse than Luna. I basically had to ran every session with a Pelican test to determine if that session is safe. So I just spun up my Claude $20 and figured that now I can get all the work done just with Opus 5. Let me show you a pelican, by &quot;gpt-6-sol&quot;. Cutting usages is one thing, but secretly downgrading models to a level that is not reliable anymore is the last straw. I am not saying other frontier labs (I am talking about you Anthropic) isn&#x27;t doing this, but their version of downgraded&#x2F;quantized&#x2F;reduced effort model is at least usable, probably just slightly dumber, OAI&#x27;s differences is day and night. <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;imgur.com&#x2F;a&#x2F;PDbYdOQ\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;imgur.com&#x2F;a&#x2F;PDbYdOQ</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:35:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790174146,"id":49816843,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Why would I ever do that to myself? My experience with Codex&#x2F;GPT is fantastic, while my impression of Claude&#x2F;Opus is that it&#x27;s longwinded, patronizing, token-inefficient, stops to ask stupid questions every other minute, overcomplicates simple tasks, often poor engineering overall. I don&#x27;t use it but this is what I see my partner run into who has access to both and compares them often. She has the same assessment.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"serf","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[{"author":"AlexErrant","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T21:35:23.000Z","created_at_i":1790199323,"id":49822908,"options":[],"parent_id":49818587,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&quot;No bitch, that&#x27;s a whole new sentence.&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:29:53.000Z","created_at_i":1790180993,"id":49818587,"options":[],"parent_id":49817160,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"So money is all that matters to you? Must be an OpenAI employee or user.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:58:00.000Z","created_at_i":1790175480,"id":49817160,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; ...if Anthropic can keep it up with this level of service...<p>fuckin laughable, literally invoked a laugh from me in real life.<p>I hope customers aren&#x27;t so stupid that they think a chatty developer on twitter&#x2F;hn&#x2F;mastodon&#x2F;screaming-in-the-wind&#x2F;wherever (or any other public-facing-place) means shit about customer service, and that goes towards <i>ANY</i> company where the primary customer service is an LLM.<p>Anthropic is the only company where it took (!) 9 weeks (!) to convince to hand over a 4 dollar refund for book-keeping errors on their side that caused an inappropriately early account deactivation due to time zone issues on their end, while all the while telling me that they don&#x27;t offer refunds. It took stacks of evidence and argument, and that was after spending two weeks in their system trying to convince every level that I was worth a human.<p>For me personally it&#x27;d require Dario to resort to armed mugging to see another buck out of my wallet. I&#x27;m not alone.<p>tl;dr : being able to convince the powers that be on highly active industry forums (hacker news, twitter, mastodon..?) to act right using the power of peer shaming doesn&#x27;t good customer service make. That said -- I do appreciate the direct response&#x2F;statement from mpoteat;<p>..I just don&#x27;t appreciate the good actions of a decent individual being too broadly interpreted as the do-good customer-centric nature of Anthropic .. an element I do not believe exists there.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"nozzlegear","children":[{"author":"evilduck","children":[{"author":"nozzlegear","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T16:51:48.000Z","created_at_i":1790268708,"id":49833434,"options":[],"parent_id":49823179,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"That&#x27;s true, but assumes that saving money is the only reason to go local (or that someone doesn&#x27;t already have the hardware to do it \u2013 a Mac with 64gb can run most 27B models). By using a local LLM, you can guarantee that your data stays private; that your workflow always works for you and won&#x27;t randomly change or stop working at the whims of an upstream provider; and that you can evolve your tools or swap in new models whenever you want, without some weird Effective Altruist culter in SF writing a dissertation on the model&#x27;s supposed mood first.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T22:01:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790200906,"id":49823179,"options":[],"parent_id":49818601,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Local is becoming ever increasingly scarce and cost prohibitive. It&#x27;s kind of bleak out there right now. A minimum bar to entry for decent local AI (something that can run a 27B tier model with some reasonable context) is going to set you back a year or five worth of AI API token costs.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:30:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790181030,"id":49818601,"options":[],"parent_id":49815520,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Do yourself a favor: ditch both and go local.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:08:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790168895,"id":49815520,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Really loved this Tibo-level responsiveness, if Anthropic can keep it up with this level of service, I am pretty sure a lot of people will just ditch their ChatGPT subscription and just move to Claude.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"grim_io","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:09:02.000Z","created_at_i":1790168942,"id":49815528,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The same guy writing readme&#x27;s for my vibeslopped toy projects is also the readme writer at Anthropic, what a coincidence ;)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"Maxion","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:09:26.000Z","created_at_i":1790168966,"id":49815534,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Well now, this is how you do community outreach","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"aviperl","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:11:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790169107,"id":49815563,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Ouch.<p>I&#x27;ve had to send such messages, but internally at work, not on HN!<p>Have a great day, human.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"OtherShrezzing","children":[{"author":"anon48293","children":[{"author":"callmeal","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:24:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790184298,"id":49819527,"options":[],"parent_id":49816564,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"don&#x27;t forget the &quot;auto reset all consent flags to &#x27;allowed&#x27;&quot; oopsie bug.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:16:56.000Z","created_at_i":1790173016,"id":49816564,"options":[],"parent_id":49815585,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Or add one additional telemetry metric and an extra prompt","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:13:36.000Z","created_at_i":1790169216,"id":49815585,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt;Apologies again folks, this was a fully human error on my part<p>Blink twice if you need help","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"fg137","children":[{"author":"rachr","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:30:14.000Z","created_at_i":1790170214,"id":49815845,"options":[],"parent_id":49815655,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The correct design was in the AGENTS.md but they didn&#x27;t have telemetry on","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:18:20.000Z","created_at_i":1790169500,"id":49815655,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; a fully human error<p>Would be interesting to know how much time you&#x2F;your team spent on that design decision","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"senko","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:35:31.000Z","created_at_i":1790170531,"id":49815939,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I hope disabling &#x2F;r if telemetry is disabled is also unintentional...","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mort96","children":[{"author":"ako","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:39:31.000Z","created_at_i":1790170771,"id":49816004,"options":[],"parent_id":49815956,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I was probably an agent that made the change, and the same agent that commented here on HN.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"criley2","children":[{"author":"mort96","children":[{"author":"_vertigo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:42:20.000Z","created_at_i":1790174540,"id":49816929,"options":[],"parent_id":49816572,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Clearly not Claude-speak, see the rest of the message. &quot;Rollout artifact&quot; just means &quot;an artifact of how we rolled this change out&quot; which maybe isn&#x27;t proper English but the message was obviously not written by Claude. Upgrade your Claudish detection","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"quintu5","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:00:53.000Z","created_at_i":1790186453,"id":49820053,"options":[],"parent_id":49816572,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It\u2019s a long-standing issue that disabling telemetry disabled feature-flagged features (e.g., remote control).","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:17:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790173054,"id":49816572,"options":[],"parent_id":49816399,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s clearly an unintended interaction. Nobody intended for the telemetry switch to control whether it reads AGENTS.md (hence mpoteat&#x27;s apologetic response). Whether you consider that to be a &quot;bug&quot; or not really wasn&#x27;t the point of my message.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"chrisjj","children":[{"author":"criley2","children":[{"author":"chrisjj","children":[{"author":"criley2","children":[{"author":"chrisjj","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T13:37:40.000Z","created_at_i":1790257060,"id":49830412,"options":[],"parent_id":49829291,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"No omission seen in this case, though.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mort96","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T14:36:32.000Z","created_at_i":1790260592,"id":49831240,"options":[],"parent_id":49829291,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Design bugs are still bugs","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T11:43:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790250237,"id":49829291,"options":[],"parent_id":49827838,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Developer comms are very important. I&#x27;ve often &quot;fixed&quot; something that was working exactly as the designer made it. It certainly wasn&#x27;t a bug in my work though. I&#x27;ve worked in places where we call this a &quot;design omission&quot; ;)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T08:27:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790238447,"id":49827838,"options":[],"parent_id":49824398,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; They&#x27;re not fixing it<p>&quot;It&#x27;s already been fixed as part of v2.1.281 releasing today.&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:00:28.000Z","created_at_i":1790208028,"id":49824398,"options":[],"parent_id":49817983,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"They&#x27;re not fixing it, they&#x27;re &quot;changing&quot; it, which makes sense, because the design changed.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:52:56.000Z","created_at_i":1790178776,"id":49817983,"options":[],"parent_id":49816399,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; That&#x27;s &quot;Working As Designed\u2122&quot;.<p>You must be baffled by the fact they&#x27;re fixing it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:05:56.000Z","created_at_i":1790172356,"id":49816399,"options":[],"parent_id":49815956,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I don&#x27;t think &quot;bug&quot; is the correct term. They put a feature behind a feature flag, and feature flags don&#x27;t work if you turn them off (via telemetry). That&#x27;s &quot;Working As Designed\u2122&quot;.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"bbor","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:41.000Z","created_at_i":1790176001,"id":49817302,"options":[],"parent_id":49815956,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Feels pretty normal to me, IDK. &quot;Rollout&quot; is definitely what was happening here, and this leftover problem can be described as an &quot;artifact&quot; most generally - I guess otherwise it&#x27;d be a... just &quot;problem&quot; or &quot;mistake&quot;? Cause &quot;bug&quot; doesn&#x27;t really fit. Plus, the Claudism here would definitely involve &quot;soak&quot;, and possibly even &quot;wall-time&quot; lol<p>IMHO it&#x27;s worth keeping in mind that Anthropic employees are some of the <i>least</i> likely to casually pass off artificial prose as authentic, given the company&#x27;s ethos&#x2F;brand&#x2F;cover story (depending on how cynical you are). To them this is all getting pretty high stakes pretty damn quickly; based on my usage of full strength Opus 5.5 today, I can&#x27;t even imagine what working with their full internal stack must feel like. If they were willing to let the machines speak for them, they&#x27;d all be melancholically lounging around home by now instead of coming in to work!<p>...I am refusing to consider the fact that they probably are still WFH because of Salesforce forcing their shared security contractor to strike. Call that a mental health ignorance on my part :)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:36:31.000Z","created_at_i":1790170591,"id":49815956,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&quot;Rollout artifact&quot;? This is Claude-speak isn&#x27;t it? I have never ever heard anyone call a bug like this a &quot;rollout artifact&quot; before.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"davidmurdoch","children":[{"author":"quintu5","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:57:54.000Z","created_at_i":1790186274,"id":49820006,"options":[],"parent_id":49816336,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"If it\u2019s like other CC features that depend on telemetry being enabled, disabling telemetry will turn off the feature.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:02:22.000Z","created_at_i":1790172142,"id":49816336,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"How are you planning to turn this off remotely when telemetry off?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"h1fra","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:26:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790173585,"id":49816717,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"people are overeacting","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mococa","children":[{"author":"samyar","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:02:26.000Z","created_at_i":1790175746,"id":49817231,"options":[],"parent_id":49817046,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"valid","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:48:27.000Z","created_at_i":1790174907,"id":49817046,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&quot;Claude, deploy yourself to a bunch of idiots, f** the bugs&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"saadn92","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:02:05.000Z","created_at_i":1790175725,"id":49817228,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Thanks for admitting to the mistake, but my understanding was that coding was fully solved now?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"lukewarm707","children":[{"author":"harry19023","children":[{"author":"lukewarm707","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[{"author":"lukewarm707","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[{"author":"lukewarm707","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T23:58:39.000Z","created_at_i":1790207919,"id":49824371,"options":[],"parent_id":49824288,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It&#x27;s a bit crazy to expect me to limit the service and expectations of everyone else for your ideals.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T23:49:54.000Z","created_at_i":1790207394,"id":49824288,"options":[],"parent_id":49820020,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Sounds like you&#x27;re no better than the big software co&#x27;s. Worse, even! I&#x27;m glad you don&#x27;t make my browser.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:58:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790186338,"id":49820020,"options":[],"parent_id":49818632,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"according to me, you have had enough screen time today and would be better not to comment. therefore, i am turning off your browser. since i am on holiday tomorrow, you will get it back next week.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:31:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790181118,"id":49818632,"options":[],"parent_id":49817687,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Sounds like you should use opensource software then. It&#x27;s a bit crazy to expect companies to limit the service and expectations of everyone else for your ideals.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dannyw","children":[{"author":"lukewarm707","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:56:35.000Z","created_at_i":1790186195,"id":49819985,"options":[],"parent_id":49819919,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"i use chrome enterprise. i control the flags from admin console.<p>EDIT: i do not control the flags from admin console. holy shit.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:51:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790185918,"id":49819919,"options":[],"parent_id":49817687,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Do you use chrome? Check chrome:&#x2F;&#x2F;flags","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:34:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790177655,"id":49817687,"options":[],"parent_id":49817486,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"how strange.<p>as i said in another comment. i don&#x27;t want someone to toy with my software remotely. that seems wrong to me!<p>i do not like others to decide that they know what is best for me. and then force it on me without my consent.<p>i will decide if i like your changes. if i do like your fix, i will install it.<p>in my car, do not remotely turn off my air conditioning. don&#x27;t turn off my AGENTS.md.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:20:14.000Z","created_at_i":1790176814,"id":49817486,"options":[],"parent_id":49817262,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"yes? feature flags have been a thing for a long time.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:04:25.000Z","created_at_i":1790175865,"id":49817262,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"is it common to deploy software with a remote kill switch installed?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dotancohen","children":[{"author":"post-it","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:23:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790176990,"id":49817527,"options":[],"parent_id":49817303,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Not necessarily. They probably have an integrated service that handles some telemetry and also feature flags, like Braze. They toggled the whole thing off based on telemetry settings. It&#x27;s a bug I&#x27;ve made before too.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"stravant","children":[{"author":"VulgarExigency","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:24:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790180686,"id":49818489,"options":[],"parent_id":49818147,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Desktop software is like web-based software, except there&#x27;s no sandbox or anyone trying to protect your privacy.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:04:18.000Z","created_at_i":1790179458,"id":49818147,"options":[],"parent_id":49817681,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I&#x27;ve used feature flags extensively throughout my career as a SaaS developer, but I&#x27;ve never considered their usage in desktop software. Not sure how I feel about it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:33:36.000Z","created_at_i":1790177616,"id":49817681,"options":[],"parent_id":49817303,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"That&#x27;s just how big companies roll out software changes for software that auto-updates.<p>It&#x27;s much preferable to be able to instantly fix it if the rollout of a new feature goes wrong than have everyone who installed the broken version bring stuck with problems until the company realizes the issue and rolls forwards with a fixed version.<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;martinfowler.com&#x2F;articles&#x2F;feature-toggles.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;martinfowler.com&#x2F;articles&#x2F;feature-toggles.html</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"dannyw","children":[{"author":"lbourdages","children":[{"author":"lionkor","children":[{"author":"lbourdages","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T18:50:04.000Z","created_at_i":1790275804,"id":49835180,"options":[],"parent_id":49824175,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"There is a meaningful difference between a generic &quot;load all flag values&quot; call that is identical for all users and some actual telemetry which sends application context to the back-end.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T23:35:57.000Z","created_at_i":1790206557,"id":49824175,"options":[],"parent_id":49824087,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Well yes but as soon as you log this on the backend, you have telemetry, no?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T23:26:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790205984,"id":49824087,"options":[],"parent_id":49819746,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"You can have flags work in a pull fashion, though. At boot, and every 5 minutes, query an endpoint which returns flag values. You don&#x27;t need the client to send any information about what the user is doing.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:40:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790185217,"id":49819746,"options":[],"parent_id":49817303,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I\u2019d just assume good intent here. Feature flags, telemetry, and fast rollouts &#x2F; rollbacks are standard practice in software. Have a look at chrome:&#x2F;&#x2F;flags perhaps.<p>I fully believe GP that there was zero intent to gate this behind collecting telemetry. Sounds like a little tech debt and a little oversight, and the simplest explanation is that it is.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"tyre","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T21:29:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790198974,"id":49822851,"options":[],"parent_id":49817303,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Seems like they overloaded whatever they use for telemetry to do feature flags.<p>It\u2019s not a crazy conspiracy. They messed up, it\u2019s fine.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790176007,"id":49817303,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"So what Anthropic calls &quot;telemetry&quot; is really &quot;telechangeability&quot;? That&#x27;s sits with me even less comfortably than did the idea that some features are only available with telemetry enabled.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"owebmaster","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:33:03.000Z","created_at_i":1790181183,"id":49818651,"options":[],"parent_id":49817666,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Lol that&#x27;s literally the entire point of the software, you install it just so the program can talk to a remote server to make changes on your local computer.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:32:45.000Z","created_at_i":1790177565,"id":49817666,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"telling people Anthropic remote-control their users computers isn&#x27;t the smartest thing to do","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"yangcheng","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:38:15.000Z","created_at_i":1790177895,"id":49817749,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"is there reason I can&#x27;t update claude to 2.1.281? I just run claude update<p>&gt; claude update\nCurrent version: 2.1.280\nChecking for updates to latest version...\nClaude Code is up to date (2.1.280)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"baq","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:48:31.000Z","created_at_i":1790178511,"id":49817907,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"It was obvious this was the reason, it\u2019s a very easy thing to forget about","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"saghm","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:42:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790181737,"id":49818811,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I can understand honest mistakes, but like, usually when I develop anything with agents (which I assume is what you&#x27;re doing internally at Anthropic), they&#x27;re almost <i>too</i> enthusiastic about trying to add test cases to the point where they sometimes try to glue together things in ways that are structurally impossible in the actual code in order to try to test that behavior. I&#x27;m honestly a bit mystified that adding a new feature didn&#x27;t get bundled in with tests that the feature works for arbitrary configurations.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"crossroadsguy","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:24:07.000Z","created_at_i":1790184247,"id":49819511,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Hey, it seems you work there. I had a tangential question. Did any Anthropic exec threaten to do something unsavoury if any engineer ever tried to not name the claude cli binary as the version number itself? Because if they did, I&#x27;d understand. Or if you dare change it all the vibe-coded ts&#x2F;react&#x2F;etc dominoes will go for a fall in unison? I&#x27;d understand that too.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"troupo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:14:52.000Z","created_at_i":1790190892,"id":49821071,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt; Sorry folks, this is a rollout artifact<p>Aka: &quot;an issue even a junior would&#x27;ve spotted if we didn&#x27;t rely on Claude of 100% of our tasks&quot;","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"PunchyHamster","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:46:20.000Z","created_at_i":1790210780,"id":49824730,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"there is a thing apps have called configuration file.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"evntdrvn","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T13:36:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790256984,"id":49830390,"options":[],"parent_id":49815363,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Shouldn&#x27;t feature flags be independent of telemetry on&#x2F;off? I would be real surprised if folks who have telemetry disabled would be upset if &quot;required-for-software-to-function-normally&quot; functionality like feature flagging itself was gated behind telemetry disablement.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:56:30.000Z","created_at_i":1790168190,"id":49815363,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Sorry folks, this is a rollout artifact, we needed a way to turn this off remotely via feature flags if it broke something, and with telemetry off you don&#x27;t get those. It&#x27;s already been fixed as part of v2.1.281 releasing today.<p>The mod is source available here: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;tree&#x2F;main&#x2F;mods&#x2F;agents-md\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;anthropics&#x2F;claude-code&#x2F;tree&#x2F;main&#x2F;mods&#x2F;age...</a><p>Apologies again folks, this was a fully human error on my part - I should&#x27;ve found a better way to launch with a kill-switch.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mgaldys4","children":[{"author":"tehlike","children":[{"author":"chrisweekly","children":[{"author":"tehlike","children":[{"author":"chrisweekly","children":[{"author":"mgaldys4","children":[{"author":"tehlike","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T06:56:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790232977,"id":49827159,"options":[],"parent_id":49826385,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I must have misremembered. I wish you kept the original though.<p>Because &quot;Even if this was an honest rollout mistake&quot; this is a new addition, changes meaning quite a bit.<p>I disagree with what you wrote now partially (your comment on claude), but it does sound fair, and i wouldn&#x27;t have written what i wrote.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T04:50:10.000Z","created_at_i":1790225410,"id":49826385,"options":[],"parent_id":49820832,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"My only edit was to continue refuting at the beginning of the sentence that Claude Code&#x27;s use of remote control to control agent.md is still incorrect. The rest is identical to the original, and my attitude before and after has not changed.<p>As for whatever &quot;had enough&quot; he mentioned, I&#x27;m not sure whether he said it on purpose or genuinely misremembered.<p>Since that&#x27;s how he remembers it, so be it. I can&#x27;t be bothered to explain anymore.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:58:58.000Z","created_at_i":1790189938,"id":49820832,"options":[],"parent_id":49816793,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Ah, thanks for clarifying. (And shame on the GP.)","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:31:59.000Z","created_at_i":1790173919,"id":49816793,"options":[],"parent_id":49816356,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The person had something else before they edited. They were overly negative, saying (from my memory) that it was inexcusable, and they had enough, pointing to malice.<p>The response as it is now sounds fair. Before that it was not.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:03:59.000Z","created_at_i":1790172239,"id":49816356,"options":[],"parent_id":49815525,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I&#x27;m not the person you replied to, but your response misses their point: rollout issue aside, the approach is flawed by design. The feature author didn&#x27;t address that at all.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"lukewarm707","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:17:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790176644,"id":49817450,"options":[],"parent_id":49815525,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"it is indefensible.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:08:56.000Z","created_at_i":1790168936,"id":49815525,"options":[],"parent_id":49815398,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Not everything is malicious. The author of the feature already responded on why this happened","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:59:14.000Z","created_at_i":1790168354,"id":49815398,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Even if this was an honest rollout mistake, the design is indefensible. Reading a local file should never depend on a remote feature flag, and silently skipping it with no warning is worse. I&#x27;ve tried to give Claude Code the benefit of the doubt, but this crosses a line.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"arrowsmith","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:00:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790168446,"id":49815417,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Claude Code also doesn&#x27;t read AGENTS.md by default if there&#x27;s a CLAUDE.md it can read instead. This isn&#x27;t limited to your repo, e.g. if you have a ~&#x2F;CLAUDE.md then no AGENTS.md will be read.<p>To always read both, you have to switch the &#x27;Project instructions&#x27; setting to the non-default `claude-md-and-agents-md`.<p>Just in case anyone is wondering why their AGENTS.md still isn&#x27;t being read.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"gmponyo","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:09:46.000Z","created_at_i":1790168986,"id":49815538,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This is not the only case where Anthropic has done stuff silently without giving users any information about changes that would hurt them.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"cowpig","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:14:03.000Z","created_at_i":1790169243,"id":49815592,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The number of people raw-dogging software that executes arbitrary instructions on their machine coming from a 3rd party server just absolutely baffles me.<p>The same people who&#x27;ve spent years of their career making sure that never happens.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"pmlnr","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:15:33.000Z","created_at_i":1790169333,"id":49815609,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Urm... no tests caught this? How?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"msp26","children":[{"author":"pszypowicz","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:21:41.000Z","created_at_i":1790173301,"id":49816640,"options":[],"parent_id":49815642,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Yeah, no thank you. This was why I polished my setup for VPN -&gt; SSH -&gt; [MOSH] -&gt; TMUX -&gt; claude&#x2F;codex","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:17:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790169444,"id":49815642,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Claude Code Remote control only works with telemetry enabled too.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"fg137","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:43:17.000Z","created_at_i":1790170997,"id":49816065,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"This in some way sounds like VSCode&#x27;s bug of always adding Copilot as a co-author of git commit regardless of user settings.<p>If people only glance over the code agents generate for them and don&#x27;t bother to spend even half a minute thinking through what&#x27;s actually happening, this is inevitable.<p>Certainly this kind of things happened before LLMs existed. But I&#x27;m not optimistic about the direction of how things are going.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"BiteCode_dev","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T13:58:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790171935,"id":49816293,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Anyway, my claude.md contains only this:<p>@agents.md","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"ChrisArchitect","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:22:24.000Z","created_at_i":1790173344,"id":49816653,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Related:<p><i>Claude Code now reads AGENTS.md if there is no Claude.md</i><p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49760187\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49760187</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"quintu5","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:28:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790173735,"id":49816756,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"And I\u2019m sure there\u2019s no conceivable way an organization as well resourced as Anthropic can separate out feature flags from telemetry. It\u2019s just too complicated! Maybe when we get AGI?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"jdlyga","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:34:13.000Z","created_at_i":1790174053,"id":49816816,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"You&#x27;re absolutely right! AGENTS.md shouldn&#x27;t be gated behind telemetry on","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"shermantanktop","children":[{"author":"throwuxiytayq","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:08:28.000Z","created_at_i":1790176108,"id":49817332,"options":[],"parent_id":49816940,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Meanwhile, Codex devs just merge their changes and hit the release button. If a thingy breaks, they fix the thingy and release a hotfix. How irresponsible! It\u2019s a miracle the software works at all!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"petters","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:13:31.000Z","created_at_i":1790176411,"id":49817398,"options":[],"parent_id":49816940,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Exactly! I can not believe this is in the top spot.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:42:54.000Z","created_at_i":1790174574,"id":49816940,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I don\u2019t understand why people are confused about the use of a launch flag, for this and for anything.<p>It\u2019s a simple distributed systems problem.  Separate the deployment of a new software feature (to umpteen hosts) from the triggering of that software with a lightweight switch.<p>If someone think that reading AGENTS.md is always benign, because they can\u2019t imagine how it could be a problem\u2026users are very creative.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"sschueller","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:51:53.000Z","created_at_i":1790175113,"id":49817090,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"If they can&#x27;t even get this simple thing right, I am worried about the future of anthropic&#x27;s products.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"mrguyorama","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[{"author":"zahlman","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[{"author":"zahlman","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[{"author":"zahlman","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-26T19:42:18.000Z","created_at_i":1790451738,"id":49859855,"options":[],"parent_id":49834203,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The part that I quoted from you clearly violates the guidelines.<p>I think the guidelines are a good idea and I would prefer to be in a community where they are upheld rather than one where they are not.<p>So I politely reminded you about them.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T17:42:41.000Z","created_at_i":1790271761,"id":49834203,"options":[],"parent_id":49831846,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"That&#x27;s a link to guidelines, not a reason... I&#x27;m having trouble reading your mind here, could you elaborate?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-24T15:19:49.000Z","created_at_i":1790263189,"id":49831846,"options":[],"parent_id":49824261,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"The reason is <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;newsguidelines.html\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;newsguidelines.html</a> .<p>There is nothing ironic about it.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T23:47:07.000Z","created_at_i":1790207227,"id":49824261,"options":[],"parent_id":49823651,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Do you have a reason, or are you ironically just putting me down because you are wanting things to be different?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T22:43:48.000Z","created_at_i":1790203428,"id":49823651,"options":[],"parent_id":49818821,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"&gt;I absolutely detest\u2026 If you [want things to work differently than how I like them], \u2026 computers are too complex for you.<p>Please don&#x27;t do this.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:42:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790181767,"id":49818821,"options":[],"parent_id":49817100,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I absolutely detest software that needs to have a configuration for every single parameter. CLAUDE.md was a new concept they created, and having it local in a directory is a blessing. If you:<p>1. really REALLY care what the file name is<p>2. Can&#x27;t put in a symlink<p>3. Don&#x27;t want to write into that file to look at other files (which is the standard practice of the entire skills framework<p>4. Cannot even think to ask the model how to come up with many solutions<p>Then I postulate you should stick to the mobile app, computers are too complex for you.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:52:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790175167,"id":49817100,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Wait wait wait WAIT<p>So, these tools have a file they want to read in with some configuration.<p>That filename is <i>hardcoded</i>?<p>Fucking DOOM had a command line parameter to provide an arbitrary configuration file name!<p>That&#x27;s completely irrespective of the fact that you need a feature flag set by <i>remote infrastructure</i> to change a setting of which <i>completely local</i> file to read.<p>It&#x27;s weird, I feel like Claude would have tried to make this a configurable setting by default! Is that just not an option in JS land? Not a common pattern to have configuration in the first place? I don&#x27;t know about that, all the JS based code editors have comprehensive configuration files.<p>What the hell is going on....","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"MPSimmons","children":[{"author":"scottyah","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:36:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790181394,"id":49818711,"options":[],"parent_id":49817378,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"yes, or a symlink.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:11:34.000Z","created_at_i":1790176294,"id":49817378,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Couldn&#x27;t you just make a CLAUDE.md that says, &quot;Read AGENTS.md in this same directory&quot;?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"stravant","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:36:38.000Z","created_at_i":1790177798,"id":49817724,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"Embarrassing for HN to have a huge thread over a Feature Flag.<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;martinfowler.com&#x2F;articles&#x2F;feature-toggles.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;martinfowler.com&#x2F;articles&#x2F;feature-toggles.html</a>","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"p5v","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:16:26.000Z","created_at_i":1790183786,"id":49819386,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I\u2019ve long since been having a pro-forma CLAUDE.md, referring to @AGENTS.md in all of my projects. Still works fine.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"silverwind","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:42:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790210575,"id":49824692,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"What&#x27;s also annoying is that Claude Code now spams &quot;agents-md: no CLAUDE.md found; AGENTS.md loaded&quot; on every startup. I could just do that silently, no need to inform me that I&#x27;m using the superior file.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"iruoy","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:52:23.000Z","created_at_i":1790211143,"id":49824785,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"just support AGENTS.md and .agents&#x2F; natively. why are you building core functionality like this?","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"AbuAssar","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T13:10:55.000Z","created_at_i":1790255455,"id":49830109,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"just ditch claude.md and use the standardised agents.md already.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null},{"author":"flaburgan","children":[],"created_at":"2026-09-24T20:28:47.000Z","created_at_i":1790281727,"id":49836373,"options":[],"parent_id":49814947,"points":null,"story_id":49814947,"text":"I always start a new project with `ln -s AGENTS.md CLAUDE.MD`. Problem solved.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2026-09-23T12:15:33.000Z","created_at_i":1790165733,"id":49814947,"options":[],"parent_id":null,"points":486,"story_id":49814947,"text":null,"title":"Claude Code reads AGENTS.md only when telemetry is on [fixed]","type":"story","url":"https://blog.szypowi.cz/p/claude-code-reads-agents.md-only-when-telemetry-is-on/"}
